    "result_text": "All tests pass (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 3/3). AcceptanceTest is the only test class in the project.\n\n## Summary\n\nI added an optional `email` field to owners: syntactically validated when present, rejected with 400 when invalid, and stored/returned lower-cased.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added `email` (`type: string, format: email`, optional) to the `OwnerFields` schema, so the generated `OwnerFieldsDto`/`OwnerDto` gain the field (and an `@Email` constraint used by the PUT path's `@Valid`).\n\n2. **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 added the `email` field with `@Column(name = \"email\")`, `@Email`, and getter/setter. MapStruct's `OwnerMapper` now maps it automatically both directions (name match), so no mapper change was needed.\n\n3. **DB schemas** \u2014 added a nullable `email` column to the `owners` table in all four dialects (`h2`, `hsqldb`, `mysql`, `postgres`). H2 is the active test profile. I also gave hsqldb's positional `INSERT INTO owners VALUES (...)` seed rows an explicit column list, since a trailing column would otherwise break them.\n\n4. **`RequireOwnerFields.java`** (POST pipeline, a manual guard rather than `@Valid`) \u2014 when `email` is present and non-blank, validate it against a syntactic pattern (rejecting via the existing `RequiredFieldsException` \u2192 400) and lower-case it before persistence.\n\n5. **`ApplyOwner.java`** (PUT pipeline) \u2014 set the email on the entity, lower-cased, normalizing blank to null. Format validation on that path comes from the DTO's `@Email` via `ValidateOwner`'s `@Valid`.\n\nThe three acceptance tests \u2014 lowercasing, invalid-email rejection (400), and missing-email acceptance \u2014 all pass, and the full suite is green.",
